<section class="slide" data-page="02 / 09">
  <div class="slide-content">
    <div class="kicker">Problem framing</div>
    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <h2>Large VLMs are powerful—but impractical at the edge.</h2>
        <p class="subtitle">Mobile and low-power devices need multimodal reasoning without cloud dependency or workstation-class memory.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="metric-grid">
          <div class="metric"><strong>27.7GB</strong><span>Molmo-A1B-7B RAM requirement</span></div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>0.8GB</strong><span>SmolVLM-256M RAM at batch=1</span></div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>300×</strong><span>SmolVLM-256M surpasses larger Idefics-80B</span></div>
        </div>
        <ul class="bullets" style="margin-top:clamp(.7rem,1.4vw,1.2rem)">
          <li><b>Constraint:</b> inference memory determines deployability on smartphones and edge hardware.</li>
          <li><b>Opportunity:</b> architectural efficiency can beat raw parameter scale.</li>
          <li><b>Goal:</b> retain competitive multimodal accuracy under strict memory budgets.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" data-page="03 / 09">
  <div class="slide-content">
    <div class="kicker">Architecture overview</div>
    <h2>Image splitting → SigLIP encoder → pixel shuffle → SmolLM2.</h2>
    <div class="pipeline">
      <div class="step"><span class="num">01</span><b>Sub-images</b><span>Images are split before visual encoding.</span></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="num">02</span><b>SigLIP vision encoder</b><span>Compact encoder maps patches to visual features.</span></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="num">03</span><b>Pixel shuffle</b><span>Space-to-depth compression lowers visual tokens.</span></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="num">04</span><b>Linear projection</b><span>Features enter the language input space.</span></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="num">05</span><b>SmolLM2 backbone</b><span>Visual and text embeddings are concatenated.</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="visual-frame">
      <img src="../benchmark/assets/figure_3.jpg" alt="SmolVLM architecture figure">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" data-page="04 / 09">
  <div class="slide-content">
    <div class="row wide-left">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">Finding 1 · compute allocation</div>
        <h2>For compact LMs, the smaller vision encoder wins.</h2>
        <p class="subtitle">A 93M SigLIP-B/16 paired with a 135M LM outperforms a 428M SigLIP-SO400M with the same LM; the larger encoder only justifies its 10% parameter overhead at 1.7B LM scale.</p>
